{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/hunter-the-vigil/396822-bits-of-a-new-conspiracy-the-foundation-for-advanced-psychiatry","id":396822,"title":"Bits of a New Conspiracy: The Foundation for Advanced Psychiatry","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Hunter: The Vigil"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-02-07T15:28:42-08:00","id":396822,"title":"Bits of a New Conspiracy: The Foundation for Advanced Psychiatry","content":"<span style=\"font-family:arial\">I'm working on a Hunter Conspiracy; it's far from done but I thought I'd post some of my notes on it here for amusement/interest.</span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The human mind is a hideously complex series of mechanisms; many of its workings are still only poorly understood. Dreams, for instance, are an enigma\u2014What purpose do they serve? Is there any meaning that can be derived from them, or are they merely electrical misfirings in a tired brain?</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"font-family:arial\"><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Why did every person in the city taking that experimental new antidepressant have the same dream of a faceless woman offering them a rotten apple on the same night? Why does one of my patients have dreams of sexual encounters with people he\u2019s never met who are found strangled exactly a week later? Why does my daughter keep having nightmares about \u201cbad men made of sticks\u201d living in the basement of the house next door?<br /> <br /> Monsters leave scars. Some are obvious, claw marks across a chest, a missing ear, a portable dialysis machine. Others, not so much. They lurk beneath the surface, tormenting their bearers until they succumb.<br /> <br /> In the World of Darkness exists a group of academics, doctors, and therapists who wish to both study the psychology of monsters and alleviate the supernatural's detrimental effects on the human psyche. Their methods combine orthodox talk therapy and medical prescriptions with outdated psychoanalysis (Jung is quite popular), arcane rituals borrowed from cultures around the globe, less-than-legal substances, and, occasionally, ethically dubious surgeries (what does it really <i>mean</i> to lobotomize a walking corpse, anyway?).</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The psychotherapists of the Foundation for Advanced Psychiatry hold their Vigil in the realms of human consciousness, fighting against the hobgoblins hiding in the brain\u2019s nooks and crannies. They\u2019ve dedicated themselves to opposing monsters on the psychological front, using group psyche as a weathervane, healing those who\u2019ve grown deranged in the face of what\u2019s out there, and sifting through dreams to find the answers they seek.<br /> <br /> <b>The Enemy</b></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Foundation behaviorists have come to recognize a handful of psychological patterns indicative of monstrous incursion. Though someone suddenly acting out of the ordinary is certainly worth investigating, what\u2019s even more troubling, often, is when someone prone to erratic behavior or mental instability suddenly takes an unexpected turn for the better, becoming serene, more confident, better put together. Hypnotherapy sessions have revealed subjects claiming to have signed away their troubles to fallen angels, let alien spirits enter their souls, or even come to the realization that they\u2019re not actually human, but merely a replacement for someone who\u2019ll be coming back soon.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mass hysteria can often be spotted in advanced, especially when local therapists decide to break patient-doctor confidentiality and compare notes, and, lo and behold, an impossible number of people have confessed to fantasizing about murdering the prostitute who hangs out on State and 14th. Sudden upswings in religious convictions are also notable, but going wisdom is to proceed cautiously and prepare to abandon ship should any patient start waxing poetically about the Fertile Crescent (though damned if anyone in the Foundation can figure out why).</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:30:33-08:00","id":396842,"title":"","content":"<b>Hunters</b><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You\u2019re a psychology professor at a small university. You\u2019ve always kept in contact with a college friend of yours who\u2019d decided to take the psychiatrist\u2019s route instead. One day you get an email from her about a strange man who claims to have gone to Mars. Then the messages stop. Then one day, out of the blue, she sends you a rambling, near-incoherent missive about discovering the secret of immortality, confessing to horrible, atrocious acts in the pursuit. Your replies go unanswered, and, deeply concerned for your friend, you reach out to your academic contacts to see if anyone knows anything about this kind of pathology. Soon after you get a response, from a research group you\u2019ve never heard of before; there\u2019s nothing that can be done for your friend now, but, if you\u2019re willing, they can show you how to keep the madness from spreading. It doesn\u2019t hurt that they\u2019re offering you funding, either.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">When you started your internship with the psych group, they gave you a bunch of required reading, including scans of Jung\u2019s private journals, nigh-incoherent anti-psychiatry screeds, even an annotated copy of </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">House of Leaves</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">. You thought it was some sort of prank on the new guy at first, but now you know they\u2019re deadly serious.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You work as a sales rep for a pharmaceutical company that specializes in mood stabilizers. You can practically feel the waves of loathing coming off the doctors when you hang around their hospitals for too long, but you\u2019re not just profiting off human misery; you\u2019ve been taking notes on who\u2019s taking what and how it\u2019s affecting them. You\u2019re saving lives and not even taking the credit. You\u2019re basically a martyr, you know.<br /> <br /> You were an orderly at a severely-underfunded state asylum, and you\u2019ve seen some shit. Not just the way the patients were neglected, or the permanent air of uncleanliness that hung over the place, but you\u2019d heard stories. Stories of nightly abuse. Stories the doctors wrote off as mass delusion. Sometimes you wish you hadn\u2019t stuck around that night and seen that pale man bite into the neck of a strapped-down inmate, but at least you\u2019re not changing bedpans anymore.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You studied philosophy, and pretty much everything you knew about mental illness came from Deleuze and Guattari. You were doing research for your senior thesis on </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Anti-Oedipus</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> when you came across the strange book stashed behind the encyclopedias. It was some arcane text from the fifties about things like \u201cDreams of Lilith\u201d and \u201cThe Ruinous Prince.\u201d There was no frontispiece, no ISBN, just a mailing address written in minuscule letters on the back of the title page. You were fascinated and decided to write your thesis on </span></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><i><span style=\"font-size:15px\">that</span></i></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> instead. When you were all but laughed out of your defense, you decided to send a letter to the address. Now who\u2019s laughing? Not you, definitely.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:31:23-08:00","id":396843,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Status</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u25cf</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> You\u2019ve been approved as a member of the Foundation and can purchase dots in the ??? Endowment.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">You\u2019ve experienced enough of the supernatural by this point, either firsthand or through your patients, that you\u2019ve trained your mind to resist outside influence. Gain the Indomitable merit. If you already have the merit, or if you purchase it later, increase its bonus by 2.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf </span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Once you\u2019ve reached this level of prestige within the Foundation, you gain access to the connections and inroads the Conspiracy has fostered with psych institutions around the globe. Whenever you make contact for the first time with an institution connected to psychological research or mental health\u2014such as a university, hospital, or insane asylum\u2014you gain access to four merit dots to divide among Allies, Contacts, Library, Mentor, Resources, Retainer, Safe Place, and Staff as you wish. Once these dots are in place for any given institution, they can\u2019t be reassigned without significant social effort.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Example: Doctor Felipe Wu\u2019s theories of the mind are renowned among both the Foundation and the wider scientific world. When reports of strange and erratic behavior among a large number of inhabitants of Sacramento cross his desk, he decides to go investigate firsthand. He initially checks in with the University of California\u2019s psych department to get a feel for what\u2019s going on. Thanks to the efforts of local members of the Foundation, Dr Wu can take advantage of some bits of the department\u2019s infrastructure; he gains four merit dots to allocate. His player decides to put two dots into Library (Science), representing a berth of books provided for him, one dot into Safe Place, as an office the department allows him to use, and one dot into Retainer, representing the psychology undergrad Rebecca Schulz, who\u2019s excited for the opportunity to intern with one of her chosen field\u2019s great minds.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Later, following up on a lead, Wu goes to the city psychiatric hospital. Again, he gains four merit dots; this time his player puts all four into Mentor. The director of the hospital, Dr Angela Harper-Roth, turns out to be another member of the Foundation, and is happy to give Felipe Wu any advice she can about Sacramento\u2019s goings-on.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T15:32:09-08:00","id":396845,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Endowment: ???</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Mental Health (\u25cf - \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Those affected by the supernatural often require specialized care. With the Mental Health Endowment, a member of the foundation can provide her patients with preventative measures and follow-up therapy for traumatic brushes with things lurking in the shadows. A therapist can have a number of patients in her care equal to her combined dots in Mental Health + Status (Foundation)\u2014maintaining patients requires time and resources, after all. Bringing a new patient into one\u2019s care requires a point of Willpower and a successful Intelligence + Medicine/Occult/Science roll to get a bead on which treatments would be the most effective. Most Foundation psychologists use a combination of talk therapy and prescription medication, though others incorporate more arcane or unorthodox practices into their sessions, such as Jungian dream interpretation, Buddhist meditation, or entheogenic rituals. Anyone under the therapist\u2019s care receives the Foundation member\u2019s dots in Mental Health as a bonus on rolls to resist mental or emotional coercion, such as a vampire\u2019s powers to rewrite memories, or a faerie\u2019s uncanny ability knack to manipulate desires. If the power in question is resisted rather than contested, subtract Mental Health from the monster\u2019s roll. Dots in Mental Health are also applied to Breaking Point rolls directly caused by a supernatural source.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Drawback: If a member of the Foundation isn\u2019t available for sessions, patients might suffer a relapse. After a number of weeks equal to the therapist\u2019s dots in Mental Health have passed without a session, a patient loses access to the Endowment\u2019s benefit.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Shock Therapy (\u25cf - \u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf\u25cf)</span></b></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Out in the field, there\u2019s not always time to talk it out. Sometimes what someone needs to snap out of hysteria is a moment of moral support, a quick dose of morphine, or maybe just a slap in the face.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Cost: 1 Willpower</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dice Pool: Wits + Medicine + Shock Therapy. If the Condition in question was caused by a supernatural power, then a Clash of Wills ensues.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Action: Instant</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Roll Results</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Dramatic Failure: You\u2019ve managed to make things worse. Choose one: You gain the same (or a similar) Condition you were trying to fix, or the patient gains a second Condition of the Storyteller\u2019s choosing.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Failure: The quick fix isn\u2019t working. You can try again, but each successive attempt nets a cumulative -1 penalty to the roll.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Success: You get the unbalanced individual to snap out of it. Success on the roll either completely absolves someone of a temporary mental or emotional Condition (such as Shaken), or suppresses a Persistent Condition (such as Addicted) for a scene. Removing a Condition this way does not garner the victim a Beat. A Persistent Condition can only be subject to Shock Therapy if the possessor is currently actively suffering from it; if an alcoholic isn\u2019t currently being tempted to drink, then there\u2019s nothing she needs to snap out of.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Exceptional Success: The patient gains the Steadfast Condition.</span></span></span><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Note: Shock Therapy works equally well on positive mental/emotional Conditions like Inspired.</span></span></span>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:01:39-08:00","id":396876,"title":"","content":"Not well read enough to talk about the mechanics, but I love the idea. It fills a decidedly needed niche, both in the thematic &quot;psychology of the supernatural&quot; front, but also in the in-narrative &quot;Who keeps your average Hunter, who suffers more than most mentally and physically from going berserk and shooting up town hall?&quot; concern. Just curious: if they were approached by a supernatural, one who wasn't evil but just wanted help with their problems, would they treat them or &quot;treat&quot; them?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3514-zealouschristian24","name":"ZealousChristian24","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1796"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-07T16:23:04-08:00","id":396895,"title":"","content":"I'm glad you like the base idea. The mechanics probably need a lot of polishing, once I actually finish a first draft. (The Status-5 benefit just came to me while I was in the shower this morning and I wanted to get it all down before I forgot.)<br /> <br /> As for your question: I suppose it would depend on some different variables, like the Integrity of the Foundation member in question, what sort of research could lead to a publishable paper (I imagine they have their own scientific journal, in the same vein as Null Mysteriis or those other mad psychologists), things like that. I haven't quite figured out their overall moral fiber yet.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-02-08T14:36:20-08:00","id":398065,"title":"","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Stereotypes</span></b></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">Hotel Mascaron:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> I was treating a woman once who\u2019d been suffering from paranoid delusions and fugue states. She was convinced that there were alien invaders from another dimension kidnapping people and replacing them with identical copies. And whenever she dreamed about the invaders, she\u2019d always wake up miles away from her house. My treatments didn\u2019t seem to be working for her, no matter what I tried. Then, she just stopped coming to sessions. After the third missed session, I got a phone call, late at night; there was a lot of static on the other end, and a strange voice said that my services were no longer needed, but thank you anyway. I thought I saw the woman again, once, but it was dark out, and she was wearing some kind of fox mask. I think she had a baseball bat with her, too. I don\u2019t know what\u2019s going on, but I think I\u2019d rather just wash my hands of it.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Loyalists of Thule:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> Guilt complexes are sometimes associated with post-traumatic stress disorder, but I\u2019m starting to wonder if my contacts in the group are hiding their true motivations for the work they\u2019re doing. They have the most awful dreams, too: mass genocides, brutal totalitarian regimes, an ancient island holding long-forgotten horrors rising from the seas...</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><b><span style=\"font-size:15px\">The Season Letters:</span></b></span></span><span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:Arial\"><span style=\"font-size:15px\"> It\u2019s funny, the only reason I got involved in all this is because of a wrong address. Back when I was an undergrad, I got a letter from someone\u2014an anthropologist, I think\u2014claiming he felt he was on the brink of making an important discovery about some sort of tribe out in California. He\u2019d included some newspaper clippings about Humboldt squid swarms and weird graffiti that was attributed to a new gang in the area. I wrote him back saying that I\u2019d received the letter by mistake, but he never replied. I wonder what happened to him? And why do some of my patients have dreams with that same graffiti?<br /> <br /> <b>VASCU:</b> I'm apparently on some sort of government file, because these guys keep getting referred to my clinic. I'd be happy to help if they ever actually let me inside their heads; they're always so cagey about their feelings. High-strung too. A lot of them suffer from imposter syndrome, recurring nightmares, and nosebleeds, for some reason I can't quite figure out. But what's much more interesting, one of them let slip that there's apparently a high-security prison out there somewhere full of mystical serial killers. What do you think <i>their</i> psyches are like? I smell tenure.</span></span></span><br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}